      Demonstrates the correct capability-check pattern: sbi_hart_has_extension(scratch, SBI_HART_EXT_ZKR) is checked before csr_set/clear(CSR_MSECCFG, MSECCFG_SSEED/USEED). However, these MSECCFG ZKR seed bits are lost on non-retentive suspend because location #1 does not save/restore MSECCFG. On warm resume, init_warm_resume calls sbi_hart_reinit() (not sbi_hart_init()), so the ZKR seed-enable writes are never re-executed. Even though the capability check is correct at init time, the lifecycle gap means the security property (S-mode access to seed CSR) is silently lost after suspend/resume. This confirms the vulnerability pattern extends beyond ePMP to other MSECCFG-managed features.Wrote 3 report(s) → output/riscv-iopmp/pr-139/

