      Smepmp extension (SBI_HART_EXT_SMEPMP at line 370) is detected solely via sbi_platform_extensions_init() (line 679) which parses the device tree 'riscv,isa-extensions' string. This contrasts with SSCOFPMF (line 644-645) which uses CSR trap-and-detect probing via csr_read_allowed(CSR_SCOUNTOVF). There is a partial defense at line 704-706: MSECCFG.MML is read and checked for consistency, but this gates on the already-DT-trusted extension flag — it only catches the case where MML is spuriously set, not the case where the MSECCFG CSR itself doesn't exist. A DT that incorrectly lists 'smepmp' causes silent execution of MSECCFG CSR instructions on non-Smepmp hardware. The trap-and-detect approach used for SSCOFPMF (probing the target CSR) would be more robust but is not employed for Smepmp. The practical risk is low since MSECCFG is mandatory in ratified privileged spec versions, but the detection methodology is inconsistent.
